---
kind: lore
id: mid.fairhaven
title: Fairhaven (the day care, the lighthouse, the Dex rater)
---

// A seaside village at the end of the Fen Walk: the day care, the old
// lighthouse, and Quill, who rates the player's Dex. Yvaine paints on the
// harbour wall at weekends.

<beat id="arrive" on="enterTown" target="town.fairhaven" title="Fairhaven" priority="10" once="run">
  ::bg{location="fairhaven" time="day"}
  ::music{action="change" mood="calm" volume="normal"}
  @narrator: Fairhaven: white cottages, a harbour full of small boats, and on the point a lighthouse that has not been lit for thirty years.
  @narrator: The day care has a fenced garden full of monsters that are not anybody's, for now. Two old people are counting them. Then counting them again.
</beat>

<entry id="midFairhavenMorning" on="enterTown" target="town.fairhaven" category="bark" once="day" when="@isMorning">
  @narrator: Gulls, fishing boats heading out, and Grandma Ilse in the day care garden calling a name over and over.
</entry>

<entry id="midFairhavenDay" on="enterTown" target="town.fairhaven" category="bark" once="day" when="run.slot == 'day'">
  @narrator: The harbour is sleepy in the afternoon. Somebody's Seahorsling is doing lazy circles by the jetty.
</entry>

<entry id="midFairhavenNight" on="enterTown" target="town.fairhaven" category="bark" once="day" when="@isNight">
  @narrator: At night the dark lighthouse on the point is darker than the sky around it. Every so often, a light moves at the top. Nobody in Fairhaven looks.
</entry>

// ── services ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<beat id="center" on="heal" target="town.fairhaven" title="Monster Center" once="false">
  ::use{component="nurse" town="fairhaven"}
</beat>

<beat id="mart" on="shop" target="town.fairhaven" title="Mart" once="false">
  ::use{component="shop" stock="fairhavenStock"}
</beat>

// ── the day care ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<beat id="dayCare" on="enterPlace" target="place.fairhavenDayCare" title="Fairhaven day care" once="false">
  ::bg{location="fairhaven-day-care" time="day"}
  @narrator: A long room with a stove, two armchairs and a ledger the size of a door. Every monster that has ever stayed here is written in it, in two different hands.
</beat>

<beat id="tobbeAsks" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenDayCareMan" title="Grandpa Tobbe" priority="10" once="run">
  ::auto{character="fairhavenDayCareMan" anchor="center" action="enter"}
  @fairhavenDayCareMan{emotion="worried"}: Twenty-two in the garden, and there should be twenty-three. Our Mothfuzz has flown off again. It always heads for the Preserve. The lights, you see.
  @fairhavenDayCareMan: Ilse won't sleep till it's back. If you catch a Mothfuzz out there, would you show her? She won't know the difference. I won't tell her.
  <branch id="midDayCareAsk" prompt="Help Grandpa Tobbe?">
    <choice id="help" label="I'll look for it">
      ::accept{quest="midDayCareRunaway"}
      @fairhavenDayCareMan{emotion="happy"}: Bless you. Look in the Wildmoor Preserve, near the lamps. And mind the contest people, they'll net anything.
    </choice>
    <choice id="busy" label="Not now">
      @fairhavenDayCareMan: No, no, of course. You've your own monsters. It'll come home. It usually does.
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>

<entry id="midTobbe" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenDayCareMan" category="bark" when="quest.midDayCareRunaway.state != 'complete'">
  @fairhavenDayCareMan: We look after anyone's monster, for a small fee and a large amount of worrying. Mostly the worrying.
</entry>

<entry id="midTobbeAfter" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenDayCareMan" category="bark" when="quest.midDayCareRunaway.state == 'complete'">
  @fairhavenDayCareMan{emotion="happy"}: Twenty-three in the garden. Twenty-four, counting yours, when you visit. Ilse's asleep in her chair. First time in a week.
</entry>

<entry id="midIlse" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenDayCareLady" category="bark" when="quest.midDayCareRunaway.state != 'active'">
  @fairhavenDayCareLady: Leave a monster with us and it'll come back happier, fatter and a little bit spoiled. That's a promise.
</entry>

<entry id="midIlseWaiting" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenDayCareLady" category="bark" when="quest.midDayCareRunaway.state == 'active'">
  @fairhavenDayCareLady{emotion="worried"}: Have you seen a Mothfuzz? Fluffy, round, likes lamps, answers to nothing. It's never been gone this long.
</entry>

// ── the harbour ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<entry id="midDexRater" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenDexRater" category="bark">
  <match>
    <when test="@dexCaught >= 80">
      @fairhavenDexRater: {{@dexCaught}} kinds! I have nothing left to teach you. I'm going to sit down.
    </when>
    <when test="@dexCaught >= 40">
      @fairhavenDexRater: {{@dexCaught}} kinds. Now that's a Dex. The professor will be telling people about you.
    </when>
    <when test="@dexCaught >= 20">
      @fairhavenDexRater: {{@dexCaught}} kinds. Respectable! Try the fens at night; things come out you won't see by day.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @fairhavenDexRater: Only {{@dexCaught}} kinds? Chin up. The Wildmoor Preserve is full of bugs, and bugs count.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</entry>

<entry id="midKeeper" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenKeeper" category="bark" when="!holds('midGhostSeen', ['fairhavenLighthouse'])">
  @fairhavenKeeper: I keep the lighthouse. I don't light it. Thirty years ago the light went out on its own, and every night since, something at the top has been trying to light it again.
</entry>

<entry id="midKeeperAfter" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenKeeper" category="bark" when="holds('midGhostSeen', ['fairhavenLighthouse'])">
  @fairhavenKeeper: You saw it? The old keeper. Still on shift. Well. Somebody has to be.
</entry>

<entry id="midPainter" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenPainter" category="bark" when="!@weekend">
  @fairhavenPainter: Weekdays I teach at the school in Silvercrest. Weekends I paint the harbour. The harbour never sits still.
</entry>

<entry id="midPainterWeekend" on="talk" target="npc.fairhavenPainter" category="bark" when="@weekend">
  @fairhavenPainter: Stand still. No, over there. You're in the harbour now. I've given you a hat. You looked like you needed a hat.
</entry>
